Burnt Basque Cheesecake is not something i've made before, I love a bit if NY Cheesecake though, even love super cheap cheesecake (any cheesecake really).

So first off......yes I did indeed burn the cheesecake a little too much but you know what.....I'm ok with that. Be happy with your makes, even if not perfect. 

So now we get on to the ice cream, super creamy and luxurious lemon cheesecake ice cream with huge pieces of basque cheesecake in. This is a GORGEOUS combo, a lot of work but so worth it. 

What will you need?

The Ice Cream:
250g Mascarpone cheese 40-45% fat
150g Cream 50% fat
550g Milk 1.8% fat
150g Sugar
65g Skimmed Milk Powder
75g dextrose
5g Lemon Extract 
2g stabiliser (optional)

The Burnt Basqe Cheesecake:
600g cream cheese (e.g. Philadelphia)
4 eggs
225 g sugar
Pinch of salt
40g of flour
300g double cream
5ml vanilla extract (optional)
The original recipe called for a 200c fan oven for 50-60 mins but I reckon it's closer to 180c Fan for 45 mins. 

An after thought here is maybe make a little cheesecake base using digestive/graham crakcers and butter, freeze it then break it up on the top of your serving of this amazing ice cream. 

